From 053a3221678978de03873742f2cfb703685a0fb9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tomaz Zaman <tomaz@mono.si>
Date: Tue, 28 Apr 2026 15:11:07 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] sdk_fman: MAC hash address allocation NULL check
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

MemacAddHashMacAddress dereferences the result of XX_Malloc without
checking for NULL. On allocation failure (e.g. ENOMEM under pressure
or fault injection), the next line crashes with a NULL pointer deref:

  cpu N: No memory for XX_Malloc
  Unable to handle kernel NULL pointer dereference at virtual address 0
  MemacAddHashMacAddress+0x1ec
  FM_MAC_AddHashMacAddr
  fm_mac_add_hash_mac_addr
  set_multi
  dpa_set_rx_mode
  __dev_set_rx_mode
  __dev_mc_add
  dev_mc_add
  ...

The path is reachable any time the kernel calls dev_mc_add() against
an FMAN-backed netdev — IGMP joins, IPv6 ND, the mcast-offload ADD
path, etc. — so any allocation failure in this hot codepath panics
the box.

Add the NULL check; return E_NO_MEMORY so callers (set_multi loop in
dpaa_eth) propagate the failure cleanly.
---
 .../net/ethernet/freescale/sdk_fman/Peripherals/FM/MAC/memac.c  | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/sdk_fman/Peripherals/FM/MAC/memac.c b/drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/sdk_fman/Peripherals/FM/MAC/memac.c
index 45b446d8d3bb..6b66035c6b6f 100644
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/sdk_fman/Peripherals/FM/MAC/memac.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/sdk_fman/Peripherals/FM/MAC/memac.c
@@ -798,6 +798,8 @@ static t_Error MemacAddHashMacAddress(t_Handle h_Memac, t_EnetAddr *p_EthAddr)
 
     /* Create element to be added to the driver hash table */
     p_HashEntry = (t_EthHashEntry *)XX_Malloc(sizeof(t_EthHashEntry));
+    if (!p_HashEntry)
+        RETURN_ERROR(MAJOR, E_NO_MEMORY, ("hash entry"));
     p_HashEntry->addr = ethAddr;
     INIT_LIST(&p_HashEntry->node);
 
-- 
